  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive pair is {散|ち}らす (to scatter something).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{散|ち}らばっている describes the resulting state of being scattered — things are in a scattered arrangement.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xが{散|ち}らばる: X is scattered\n- Xに{散|ち}らばる: scattered across/in X\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {書類|しょるい}が{散|ち}らばる: papers are strewn about\n- あちこちに{散|ち}らばる: scattered here and there\n- {広範囲|こうはんい}に{散|ち}らばる: dispersed over a wide area\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {散|ち}らかる: to be messy, in disarray (implies untidiness)\n- {散|ち}らばる: to be scattered, dispersed (more neutral, spatial distribution)",
